ffprobe notice
==============

Listenarr ships the ffprobe program from the Openur.FFprobeStatic NuGet package to read audio
file metadata. Listenarr runs it as a separate program and does not modify it. The package
version is pinned in Directory.Packages.props; this notice describes version 9.0.2.508.

What it is
----------

ffprobe is part of FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org). The packaged binaries report the version
"9.0.2-Openur" and were built from the FFmpeg n9.0.2 release tag with these configure options,
shared by every platform in the package:

  --extra-version=Openur --prefix=/opt/ffmpeg --enable-version3 --enable-static
  --disable-shared --enable-pic --disable-programs --disable-everything --disable-autodetect
  --disable-iconv --disable-network --disable-avdevice --disable-avfilter --disable-swresample
  --disable-swscale --disable-doc --disable-debug --enable-ffprobe --enable-protocol=file
  --enable-demuxers --enable-parsers --enable-decoders --enable-bsf=av1_frame_split
  --enable-bsf=av1_frame_merge --enable-bsf=av1_metadata --enable-libdav1d --disable-unstable

Platform builds add their own toolchain options (for example --target-os and --arch). The build
uses neither --enable-gpl nor --enable-nonfree.

Two patches are applied to the FFmpeg source before it is built:

  patches/v8.0_dts_es_audio.patch
  patches/v8.0_x2645_codec_tag.patch

The binaries are statically linked with dav1d 1.5.4 (https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav1d),
an AV1 decoder.

Licences
--------

With --enable-version3 and without --enable-gpl, FFmpeg's LICENSE.md places the build under the
GNU Lesser General Public License version 3 or later. That licence is in LGPL-3.0.txt; it
supplements the GNU General Public License version 3, which is in GPL-3.0.txt. dav1d is under
the BSD 2-Clause licence in dav1d-BSD-2-Clause.txt.

